{
  "date": "2026-10-09",
  "status": "Diagnosis only; no detector change or proposed threshold.",
  "scope": "24 cases across six development recordings: eight caught kicks, eight strict misses (one is a 53.33 ms late hit), four v5 extras with prior stem-ablation evidence and four hybrid fires in reviewed kick-free master passages.",
  "method": "Small descriptive kick failure audit. No detector, fitting or threshold sweep.\n\nPositive observations end 20/35/50 ms after a provisional label. Negative\nobservations end at an actual unwanted firing, whose acoustic onset is unknown.\nAll measurements use past samples only at that endpoint. This asymmetry is\nintentional: compare available evidence, not purportedly aligned source onsets.\n",
  "feature_order": [
    "growth_db",
    "low_fraction",
    "high_fraction",
    "spectral_change",
    "crest",
    "tail_head_db"
  ],
  "feature_definitions": {
    "growth_db": "10 log10 mean-square power ratio of current window to preceding equal window.",
    "low_fraction": "Hann FFT power from 45 to below 140 Hz divided by power from 45 to 8000 Hz.",
    "high_fraction": "Hann FFT power from 2000 to 8000 Hz divided by power from 45 to 8000 Hz.",
    "spectral_change": "1 minus cosine similarity of magnitude spectra over 45-8000 Hz in adjacent equal windows; amplitude-scale invariant.",
    "crest": "Peak absolute waveform divided by RMS in current window.",
    "tail_head_db": "10 log10 power ratio of second half to first half of current window."
  },
  "findings": [
    "All six nominal scalar feature ranges overlap between positives and negatives at each of 20, 35 and 50 ms. No one-cutoff solution is demonstrated; multivariate separation is not ruled out.",
    "The two sampled Late Night roll misses at 204.450 and 204.725 s have 50 ms average energy changes of -1.45 and -1.55 dB despite visible source/master attacks. Their existence cannot be inferred from a mandatory overall loudness increase.",
    "Inhale at 12.620 s has only +0.85 dB full-mix growth over 50 ms. The existing, hash-verified no-bass counterfactual has +14.99 dB growth and a recorded fire at 12.640 s. This supports interference/masking as a failure mechanism; subtraction changes detector state and does not prove instrument identity.",
    "The four kick-free master examples have 50 ms spectral-change values 0.008-0.067, compared with 0.260-0.743 for the 16 labelled kicks at nominal endpoints. Even with +/-20 ms positive endpoint shifts, the lowest kick value is 0.106. This narrow selected-case gap is a hypothesis for persistent-bass ghost rejection, not a validated threshold or 50 ms latency guarantee.",
    "That spectral distinction does not cover abrupt bass/drum extras: their 50 ms values span 0.188-0.633. Separate persistent-bass ghost triggers, genuine non-kick attacks, masked kicks and late decisions in subsequent diagnosis.",
    "At 20/35 ms, positive endpoint uncertainty removes the clean gap against kick-free examples. Nominal alignment alone would overstate separability."
  ],
  "visual_review": {
    "path": "/Users/peterkiemann/.cache/manifold/master-kick-comparison-2026-10-09/late_night/kick_details_2.png",
    "observation": "Existing panels 16 and 18 show kick-stem renewals within an ongoing tail and corresponding changes in the master around 204.45 and 204.725 s. These support event presence, not exact onset latency."
  },
  "next_question": "Can a causal description of spectral continuity distinguish persistent-bass modulation from a new event while preserving masked/rolling kicks? First test that limited separation on the full development passages with actual hop timing; it will not by itself classify abrupt bass notes or other drums.",
